{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO annual allowable rent increase","requirement":"For RSO-covered units a landlord may raise rent only once every 12 months and only by the allowable rent increase percentage set by LAHD; market-rate increases are allowed if the tenant voluntarily moves out, is evicted for cause, or accepts a buyout.","key_value":"once every 12 months at the allowable rent increase percentage","coverage_conditions":"Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, including apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, two or more single-family units on one parcel, hotel or rooming-house rooms occupied more than 30 consecutive days, ADUs, JADUs and mobilehomes.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Also replacement units under LAMC Section 151.28 and recreational vehicles in mobilehome parks."},"exemptions":"Condominium and townhome tenancies commenced after December 31, 1995 are not rent regulated; a landlord may apply for a Luxury Exemption based on the rent charged on or before May 31, 1978.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC ch. XV, Rent Stabilization Ordinance","quoted_span":"Rent may be increased once every 12 months by the allowable rent increase percentage","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO utility increase eliminated","requirement":"From February 2, 2026, a landlord may no longer include an additional percentage rent increase for utilities on RSO-covered rental units.","key_value":"no additional utility increase effective 2026-02-02","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-02-02","citation":"LAMC ch. XV, Rent Stabilization Ordinance","quoted_span":"Effective February 2, 2026, the landlord can no longer include an additional percentage increase for utilities.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO additional dependent increase eliminated, additional tenant 10% allowed","requirement":"From February 2, 2026 the extra 10% increase for an additional dependent is no longer permitted; a 10% increase for an additional non-dependent tenant remains allowed, within 60 days of the landlord learning of the tenant.","key_value":"10% for an additional tenant; dependent increase eliminated 2026-02-02","coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2026-02-02","citation":"LAMC ch. XV, Rent Stabilization Ordinance","quoted_span":"Effective February 2, 2026, an additonal 10% increase for an additional dependent added to the tenancy is no longer permitted. However, a 10% for an additional tenant is allowed (not a dependent) if moves into a rental unit: Landlords can increase the rent within 60 days of learning about the additional tenant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO legal reasons for eviction","requirement":"For RSO units, a landlord may end a tenancy only for listed at-fault causes such as nonpayment, lease violation, nuisance or illegal use, or no-fault causes such as owner or family move-in, resident manager, demolition, government order or conversion to affordable housing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance, generally properties first built on or before October 1, 1978.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 151.09","quoted_span":"Tenant is not at-fault

The owner or immediate family member will move into the rental unit

A resident manager will move into the rental unit

Demolition and permanent removal from the rental market

Government order

Conversion to affordable housing","interaction":"Properties not covered by the Rent Stabilization Ordinance are governed instead by the City's Just Cause Ordinance.","confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO eviction notice filing with LAHD","requirement":"A landlord must file every notice terminating the tenancy of an RSO-covered rental unit with the Los Angeles Housing Department within three business days of serving it on the tenant.","key_value":"3 business days","coverage_conditions":"All rental units subject to the City's Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC § 151.09.C.9 & § 165.05.B.5","quoted_span":"must be filed with the Los Angeles Housing Department (LAHD) within
three (3) business days of service on the tenant
per Los Angeles Municipal Code 151.09.C.9 & 165.05.B.5.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO no-fault eviction relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord carrying out a no-fault eviction of an RSO tenant must file a Landlord Declaration of Intent to Evict with LAHD, serve a 30-day and 60-day written notice, and pay tenant relocation assistance.","key_value":"relocation assistance payment for no-fault evictions","coverage_conditions":"No-fault evictions of tenants in rental units subject to the Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC ch. XV, Rent Stabilization Ordinance","quoted_span":"No-fault evictions require the payment of
relocation assistance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"RSO coverage of security deposit interest","requirement":"Interest payments on security deposits are among the matters the Rent Stabilization Ordinance covers for rental units subject to it.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units subject to the City of Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":"1978-10-01","built_after":null,"date_basis":"construction_date","min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"LAMC ch. XV, Rent Stabilization Ordinance","quoted_span":"Interest Payments on Security Deposits","interaction":null,"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
